cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AgentLeak: privacy-leakage testing for agentic AI systems"
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite both the software
  itself and the benchmark paper it implements.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Faouzi
    family-names: El Yagoubi
  - given-names: José Alejandro
    family-names: Quintero
    email: alejandro.quintero@polymtl.ca
  - given-names: Ranwa
    family-names: Al Mallah
repository-code: "https://github.com/yagobski/agentleak"
url: "https://www.agentleak.org"
abstract: >-
  AgentLeak audits a complete agent execution trace for privacy leakage across
  eight channels — user input, tool calls, tool responses, shared memory,
  inter-agent messages, logs, generated files and the final answer — and scores
  it deterministically. An agent can return a clean answer while private data
  leaves through an internal channel. Version 0.11.6 bundles 266 scenarios with
  complete source, license and attribution metadata and supports deterministic,
  NER-assisted and semantic detection tiers.
keywords:
  - privacy
  - agentic AI
  - multi-agent systems
  - data leakage
  - software testing
  - compliance
license: MIT
